      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to determine the dimensions of the backyard first. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( L \\) meters and the width by \\( W \\) meters.\n\nFirst, we know that walking the length 25 times equals 1000 meters:\n\\[ 25L = 1000 \\]\n\\[ L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNext, we know that walking the perimeter 10 times equals 1000 meters. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[ P = 2L + 2W \\]\nSo, walking the perimeter 10 times is equivalent to walking 20 meters each time. Therefore:\n\\[ 10 \\times 2L + 10 \\times 2W = 1000 \\]\n\\[ 20L + 20W = 1000 \\]\n\\[ 20(L + W) = 1000 \\]\n\\[ L + W = \\frac{1000}{20} = 50 \\]\n\\[ W = 50 - L \\]\n\nSince we already know \\( L = 40 \\):\n\\[ W = 50 - 40 = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nNow that we have the dimensions of the backyard, we can find the area \\( A \\):\n\\[ A = L \\times W = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
