      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to determine the dimensions of the backyard step by step. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( L \\) meters and the width by \\( W \\) meters.\n\nFirst, we are given that Mateen must walk the length 25 times to cover a kilometer. This information tells us:\n\\[\nL \\times 25 = 1000 \\, \\text{meters}\n\\]\nSolving for \\( L \\):\n\\[\nL = \\frac{1000 \\, \\text{meters}}{25} = 40 \\, \\text{meters}\n\\]\n\nNext, we are also given that Mateen must walk the perimeter 10 times to cover a kilometer. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[\nP = 2L + 2W\n\\]\nSubstituting the known value of \\( L \\):\n\\[\nP = 2(40) + 2W = 80 + 2W\n\\]\nWe are given that this path is 10 times the distance of the perimeter to be a kilometer:\n\\[\n10P = 1000 \\, \\text{meters}\n\\]\nSubstituting the expression for \\( P \\):\n\\[\n10(80 + 2W) = 1000\n\\]\nSolving for \\( W \\):\n\\[\n800 + 20W = 1000\n\\]\n\\[\n20W = 200\n\\]\n\\[\nW = 10 \\, \\text{meters}\n\\]\n\nNow that we have both dimensions, the area \\( A \\) of the backyard is given by:\n\\[\nA = L \\times W\n\\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( L \\) and \\( W \\):\n\\[\nA = 40 \\, \\text{meters} \\times 10 \\, \\text{meters} = 400 \\, \\text{square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{400}\n\\]",
