      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the area of Mateen's rectangular backyard, we need to find the dimensions of the rectangle. We know two things:\n\n1. Walking the length 25 times is equivalent to walking 1 kilometer.\n2. Walking the perimeter 10 times is equivalent to walking 1 kilometer.\n\nFirst, let's denote the length of the rectangular backyard by \\( L \\) meters and the width by \\( W \\) meters.\n\nFrom the first piece of information, we can write:\n\\[ 25L = 1000 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( L \\):\n\\[ L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nFrom the second piece of information, we can write:\n\\[ 10 \\times (2L + 2W) = 1000 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( 2L + 2W \\):\n\\[ 10 \\times (2L + 2W) = 1000 \\]\n\\[ 2L + 2W = \\frac{1000}{10} = 100 \\]\n\\[ L + W = 50 \\]\n\nNow we have two equations:\n1. \\( L = 40 \\)\n2. \\( L + W = 50 \\)\n\nSubstituting \\( L = 40 \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 40 + W = 50 \\]\n\\[ W = 50 - 40 = 10 \\]\n\nNow we have the dimensions of the rectangle:\n\\[ \\text{Length} = 40 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Width} = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of the rectangular backyard is given by:\n\\[ A = L \\times W = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters} \\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is:\n\\[ \\boxed{400} \\]",
