      "text": "Let $l$ represent the length of the rectangular backyard and $w$ represent the width.\n\nAccording to the given information, we have two equations:\n\n1. Walking the length 25 times: $25l = 1000$\n2. Walking the perimeter 10 times: $2(2l + 2w) = 1000$\n\nWe can solve these equations to find the values of $l$ and $w$.\n\nFrom equation 1:\n$25l = 1000 \\implies l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40$\n\nFrom equation 2:\n$2(2l + 2w) = 1000 \\implies 4l + 4w = 1000$\n\nSubstitute the value of $l$ from equation 1 into equation 2:\n$4(40) + 4w = 1000 \\implies 160 + 4w = 1000 \\implies 4w = 840 \\implies w = \\frac{840}{4} = 210$\n\nNow we can find the area of the rectangle:\nArea $= l \\times w = 40 \\times 210 = \\boxed{8400}$ square meters.\n\nThe area of Mateen's backyard is $8400$ square meters.",
